1896–97 was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic Football Club]]'s ninth season of competitive association football. They competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1890/celtic1897.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1896-97|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref>

It was the first season in the club's history in which they didn't win any trophies, neither national nor local, such as the [[Glasgow Cup]] or [[Glasgow Charity Cup]]. It was also the last season played by [[James Kelly (footballer, born 1865)|James Kelly]], Celtic's first ever captain.

